+# Independent G5 half-reference recipe
+
+Private preparation only; no selected publisher/checkpoint load, model forward, GPU/reference execution or native admission until Root releases the actual FP32 and G5 gates. Synthetic CPU-only literal controls are separate and cannot qualify a model.
+
+Only the existing authenticated original publisher owners may load actual arrays: Focus run_focus_export.py verify_assets + load_official on CPU; Context qwen3_reference_r2.py load_authenticated, strict complete index/tied-head and BF16-to-FP32 expansion. Pin their actual source hashes before invoking. Candidate ONNX graphs, exported output scores, W8-dequantized values, failed GQA/Dense or exporter conversion routines never supply expected values. Preserve existing research/model/license attribution and source receipts. This recipe has no download, tokenizer, native DTO, Profile/RuntimeManifest or qualification authority.
+
+All learned embeddings and seven projections/layer are independently rounded from original logical FP32 to half. Norm scales and Focus trained no/yes head rows2152/9693 stay finite FP32. Every learned source and rounded tensor must be finite; overflow refuses. Reject missing/extra weights, unexpected biases, unsupported rope/sliding/activation/ties, and invalid geometry. Natural publisher matrix layout is out/in; record its transpose hash separately for ONNX layout comparison without decoding ONNX outputs. Full tensor/shape/source and rounded census is required, not an FP16 label or attention-only cast.
+
+Use explicit half embedding/GEMM outputs then FP32 residual, RMSNorm epsilon1e-6, Q/K RMSNorm, SiLU/gate multiplication, noninterleaved rotate-half RoPE theta1e6 and final score arithmetic. Positions come unchanged from native compiler. Q-head width and backbone width are independent (Large Q4096 versus hidden2560). K/V heads repeat consecutively. Post-RoPE Q/K and V are half at attention entry. Independent chunked Torch FP32 QK/softmax/AV arithmetic evaluates the same causal half-input math, then rounds the attention output to half before the original FP32 output boundary. It is a reference algorithm, NOT proof of native Flash/MEA execution, latency or placement.
+
+Focus consumes the exact native three Int64 inputs, static512 left-padded nonempty suffix, original position_ids0..511 and final decision511; keep full positions during norm/RoPE before slicing the live suffix for causal reference attention. Padded query outputs are explicit zero before residual, never0*NaN. Readout is the two original FP32 head rows. Context consumes exact native six-input all-live1..8192 ABI, final decision, <=8 valid candidate vocabulary IDs and native option mask. Candidate IDs are vocabulary IDs, not token positions. Sparse rows come from the same rounded half embedding, cast only gathered rows FP32, score FP32 and retain masked -1e4.
+
+The original CompiledInput object is retained opaque and unchanged; do not rebuild a native schema, retokenize, trim, crop or fabricate a digest. Original-FP32 reference arrays may be reused only under the already reviewed exact18-row complete input/candidate/provenance equality; fresh G5 templates must repeat that full equality gate. New producer identity must truthfully state this recipe/rounding/method and preserve original producer identities for reused values. No old numeric pass, CAL/task/resource/placement/latency verdict transfers.
+
+FP32 math must disable TF32 and reduced-precision GEMM accumulation; original reference process owns startup state, environment, deadline and actual settlement. Native G5 GEMM2/debug/Flash-or-MEA math policy is a separate owner. No fake output/deadline/handle proof or within-call precision fallback. Keep frozen numeric tolerances unchanged. Actual selected-model resource bounds/CPU/GPU fit remain unknown; the8GiB export tool cap is not a full-model Torch-reference admission. Lifecycle must review actual native/reference host/device bounds and hardware claims before any selected run.
+
+Complete parameter census includes independently decoded logical original FP32 SHA and ONNX-layout FP32 SHA for every learned projection, plus rounded dtype/layout SHA. Digesting uses bounded <=4MiB contiguous row chunks, including transposed matrices; do not construct multi-GiB temporary byte arrays merely to hash. This census proves actual source/rounding correspondence only when an authorized real run emits it and native owner compares the actual exported initializer closure.
+
+The independent actual-candidate byte binder maps complete publisher parameter names to actual graph initializer consumers, reads/hashes actual half/protected ranges in bounded chunks, checks dtype/shape/no-overlap/complete floating census and compares against independently rounded publisher bytes (including transpose). Exporter-reported range digests are not accepted as observations. Actual source/graph/process fences and native graph-math admission remain with the native owner; no model inference occurs in byte binding.
